                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Balliol
                        College (Domus de Balliolo)</orgName><p>‘An erased inscription in the
                        upper margin of 46 has not been read, but does not look early. On 5 in a
                        clumsy 14th-cent. hand is: Arsmetica Boycii cum musica || Tradatur (?) hic
                        liber aule de Balliolo. On 4v is a 15th-cent. title, and on 6 two 15th-cent.
                        notes of valuation: prec. vi s. Donor unknown; possibly the copy bequeathed
                        A.D. 1372 by Simon Bredon, canon of Chichester’ (Mynors, Balliol,
                     325)</p></provenance>
